editorialMd:
The working idea

links is a symmetric 0/1 adjacency matrix. Start a depth-first traversal at each still-unvisited vertex, in increasing index order. Produce the number of vertices in each component, in that start order.

Return the sum of all values in the derived sequence; return 0 for an empty sequence.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(V^2); space O(n).

javascript
function islandLedgersTotalReceipt(links, k) {
  const a=links; let out=[];
  const n=a.length,seen=Array(n).fill(false);for(let start=0;start<n;start++){if(seen[start])continue;const stack=[start];seen[start]=true;let count=0;while(stack.length){const u=stack.pop();count++;for(let v=0;v<n;v++)if(a[u][v]&&!seen[v]){seen[v]=true;stack.push(v);}}out.push(count);}
  return out.reduce((s,x)=>s+x,0);
}


